{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew","id":1454992,"title":"[V5] More Tempting Diablerie Homebrew","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-15T14:38:51-07:00","id":1454992,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon3.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [V5] More Tempting Diablerie Homebrew","content":"Okay, so story time. I originally wanted to work on a homebrew that gave vampires access to the Elder Discipline Powers and higher attribute/skill dots. However, as I looked at multiple books such as V5 itself, VTR, and V20 I realized something: It\u2019s not needed. Okay hear me out, yes Elder Powers were just amazing, and we should have more discipline power choices but as it stands in V5, the role of Elder Powers is already handled well in the core Level 5 powers, and the higher attributes/skill dots are handled well/better with Blood Surge in this edition.<br /> <br /> With all that said, as I was working on the thought I ended up thinking about Diablerie, as you do, and how odd it is in V5. It isn\u2019t tempting enough. This is an act so awful and evil, but yet so so tempting that we should fear it. In V5, the downsides are just straight up overwhelming compared to the potential upsides. It is so bad that the few times it has happened in game; it was just sad and basically nothing happened. This annoys me, so I rewrote the rules of Diablerie a bit to make it so much more tempting for players to attempt. Keep in mind that these rules make it more tempting, but also carry at enough risk to cause some caution.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><span style=\"font-size:26px\"><u><b>Diablerie +</b></u></span><br /> The rules for committing Diablerie remain unchanged. However, the rules pertaining to the effects have been rewritten/edited to make them so much more tempting and interesting. They are as followed:<br /> <br /> \u25a0 The diablerist gains 3 stains, which can be reduced to at minimum of 1 based on the diablerist\u2019s convictions. If the diablerist accumulates more Stains than they have empty boxes on their Humanity track, they lose 1 Humanity automatically and all Stains before adding the remaining Stains to the now empty boxes.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 They must then roll a contest of Resolve + their own Blood Potency vs. the victim\u2019s Resolve + Blood Potency. Even if the diablerist fails this contest to assert control, every counted success rolled on the Humanity + Blood Potency roll gives them 5 experience points. These points can be saved for later or spent immediately, but can only be used to increase Blood Potency (to a maximum up to the victim\u2019s Blood Potency) or on disciplines known by the victim.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 Should the roll fail, the diablerist gains an additional number of stains for each success by which they failed. If the diablerist accumulates more Stains than they have empty boxes on their Humanity track, they lose 1 Humanity automatically and all Stains before adding the remaining Stains to the now empty boxes. If this would corrode their Humanity to 0 (zero), their prey\u2019s mind replaces the diablerist\u2019s; they become the host body of the Blood and personality of their target, becoming an SPC.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 If the victim was of lower generation, the diablerist lowers their generation by one for every 3 generations of difference (minimum of 1). If the diablerist was of a generation higher than 14th (Thin-Blood), they will always be considered of 14th generation for this purpose.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 Black veins become visible in the diablerist\u2019s aura. They persist for a year, or if the diablerist\u2019s generation was higher than their prey\u2019s, they persist for a number of years equal to the original difference in generation.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 The diablerist must make a Composure + Resolve roll at a difficulty of the victim\u2019s Blood Potency. On a failure, the diablerist becomes addicted to the sensation of Diablerie and the taste of vitae. From that point forward, whenever the diablerist tastes of kindred vitae they must make a Hunger Frenzy with a difficulty equal to the number of times the diablerist has commited Diablerie (This is 2 + Bane Severity + The number of past Diablerie for diablerists of clan Banu Haqim). During a hunger frenzy, even one not provoked by kindred vitae, a diablerist specifically will seek vampiric vitae first and foremost, only settling for fresh mortal blood if no avaliable kindred are in the immediate area.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":26764,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","user":"Vilenecromancer","date":".  Responding to feedback, and adjusting the idea accordingly 07-16-2021, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T00:44:46-07:00","id":1455014,"title":"","content":"Why not just use the V20 rules, or the expanded ones from Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand? They're much simpler and the benefits are pretty balanced.<br /> <br /> Perversely, your current rules make it easier to gain control if you have a higher Humanity score. That seems wrong to me. Maybe the roll should be Resolve + Blood Potency for both parties instead?<br /> <br /> As for elders, I agree that higher level Disciplines are no longer a requisite, but having ratings of 6+ would increase your dice pool and get around the limit of five powers for any Discipline. <br /> <br /> But either way, Blood Surge is not a suitable replacement for elder traits. Blood Surge only replaces blood buffing, and even then, only weakly (they lasted for a scene before, and only last for a single roll now).<br /> <br /> There was some good discussion of this elsewhere, when comparing pre-V5 Helena's traits with her new stats. Someone with trait maximums of 6-9 can have 12-18 dice in a pool--and that's on all rolls using those traits. That's much better than Blood Surge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 07-16-2021, 03:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T03:22:23-07:00","id":1455019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew#post1454992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:24px\"><u><b>Diablerie </b></u></span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u25a0 They must then roll a contest of Humanity + their own Blood Potency vs. the victim\u2019s Resolve + Blood Potency. Even if the diablerist fails this contest to assert control, every counted success rolled on the Humanity + Blood Potency roll gives them 3 experience points. These points can be saved for later or spent immediately, but can only be used to increase Blood Potency (to a maximum up to the victim\u2019s Blood Potency) or on disciplines known by the victim.</span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The XP will absolutely fuck up the balance of the party. XP in V5 is hard to obtain. Also gotta lament that you're still using humanity for the diablerists roll? So the more humane you are, the greater the benefits of diablerie? Seems a bit counter intuitive. blood potency also encourages 'eating the poor' rather than eating the rich. Why not use willpower or stamina or resolve or... Yeah, these complaints are levied at V5 too, but I'm not sure why you're continuing with them. Learn from the mistakes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u25a0 If the victim was of lower generation, the diablerist lowers their generation by one for every 3 generations of difference. If the diablerist was of a generation higher than 14th (Thin-Blood), they will always be considered of 14th generation for this purpose. </div> </div> </div>You are still going to lower gen for diablerizing someone with at least one gen lower right? It's very hard to find folks with three gens lower than yourself.<br /> <br /> .</span></div>I aprove of your humanity stains rather than auto-loss tho.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T08:24:46-07:00","id":1455026,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I like stains rather than dot loss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T08:31:03-07:00","id":1455027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1455014#post1455014\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why not just use the V20 rules, or the expanded ones from Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand? They're much simpler and the benefits are pretty balanced.<br /> <br /> Perversely, your current rules make it easier to gain control if you have a higher Humanity score. That seems wrong to me. Maybe the roll should be Resolve + Blood Potency for both parties instead?<br /> <br /> As for elders, I agree that higher level Disciplines are no longer a requisite, but having ratings of 6+ would increase your dice pool and get around the limit of five powers for any Discipline.<br /> <br /> But either way, Blood Surge is not a suitable replacement for elder traits. Blood Surge only replaces blood buffing, and even then, only weakly (they lasted for a scene before, and only last for a single roll now).<br /> <br /> There was some good discussion of this elsewhere, when comparing pre-V5 Helena's traits with her new stats. Someone with trait maximums of 6-9 can have 12-18 dice in a pool--and that's on all rolls using those traits. That's much better than Blood Surge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmmm, all good points. Although the problem with the V20 Diablerie is free stuff which V5 highly discourages since in order to cement anything you have to spend EXP on it, anything else goes away after the story is over. Otherwise I would gladely steal from V20 as I started to since I started playing V20. Also the suggestion for the roll helps a bit, I like it. Thank you very much there.<br /> <br /> As for the +6 dots I actually do agree thinking about it. If you wanted to allow high attribute dots then you could either the VTR route or traditional route for a V5 solution. If you go the VTR route then it is simple as looking at Blood Potency, and allowing their rating maximum to be equal to their Blood Potency to a minimum of 5. Example: A kindred with Blood Potency of 7 can have up to 7 points worth of dots. If their Blood Potency weakens because of time in torpor, which can happen, the rating does not lower. This is how VTR did it, and I kinda like it.<br /> <br /> Obviously traditional route is to use the generation chart from old editions and using it for the maximum.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T08:35:15-07:00","id":1455029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1455019#post1455019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\">The XP will absolutely fuck up the balance of the party. XP in V5 is hard to obtain. Also gotta lament that you're still using humanity for the diablerists roll? So the more humane you are, the greater the benefits of diablerie? Seems a bit counter intuitive. blood potency also encourages 'eating the poor' rather than eating the rich. Why not use willpower or stamina or resolve or... Yeah, these complaints are levied at V5 too, but I'm not sure why you're continuing with them. Learn from the mistakes.<br /> <br /> You are still going to lower gen for diablerizing someone with at least one gen lower right? It's very hard to find folks with three gens lower than yourself.<br /> <br /> .</span></div>I aprove of your humanity stains rather than auto-loss tho.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> These are good points, and I will be making some edits with that in mind. Also to answer the lower gen thing, the intention is there is a minimum of 1 for each attempt, but I guess I wrote it too confusingly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T09:01:35-07:00","id":1455030,"title":"","content":"I have made changes to the rules based of feedback, and will be archiving the older rules here for safe storage to show what has changed.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Version 1.0</b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><u><b>Diablerie +</b></u></span><br /> The rules for committing Diablerie remain unchanged. However, the rules pertaining to the effects have been rewritten/edited to make them so much more tempting and interesting. They are as followed:</span><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">\u25a0 The diablerist gains 3 stains, which can be reduced to at minimum of 1 based on the diablerist\u2019s convictions. If the diablerist accumulates more Stains than they have empty boxes on their Humanity track, they lose 1 Humanity automatically and all Stains before adding the remaining Stains to the now empty boxes.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 They must then roll a contest of Humanity + their own Blood Potency vs. the victim\u2019s Resolve + Blood Potency. Even if the diablerist fails this contest to assert control, every counted success rolled on the Humanity + Blood Potency roll gives them 3 experience points. These points can be saved for later or spent immediately, but can only be used to increase Blood Potency (to a maximum up to the victim\u2019s Blood Potency) or on disciplines known by the victim.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 Should the roll fail, the diablerist gains an additional number of stains for each success by which they failed. If the diablerist accumulates more Stains than they have empty boxes on their Humanity track, they lose 1 Humanity automatically and all Stains before adding the remaining Stains to the now empty boxes. If this would corrode their Humanity to 0 (zero), their prey\u2019s mind replaces the diablerist\u2019s; they become the host body of the Blood and personality of their target, becoming an SPC.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 If the victim was of lower generation, the diablerist lowers their generation by one for every 3 generations of difference. If the diablerist was of a generation higher than 14th (Thin-Blood), they will always be considered of 14th generation for this purpose.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 Black veins become visible in the diablerist\u2019s aura. They persist for a year, or if the diablerist\u2019s generation was higher than their prey\u2019s, they persist for a number of years equal to the original difference in generation.<br /> <br /> \u25a0 The diablerist must make a Composure + Resolve roll at a difficulty of the victim\u2019s Blood Potency. On a failure, the diablerist becomes addicted to the sensation of Diablerie and the taste of vitae. From that point forward, the diablerist always takes the Hunger compulsion when they suffer a bestial failure or messy critical. This in addition to the normal consequences of such results.</span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T11:29:21-07:00","id":1455033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1455027#post1455027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hmmmm, all good points. Although the problem with the V20 Diablerie is free stuff which V5 highly discourages since in order to cement anything you have to spend EXP on it, anything else goes away after the story is over. Otherwise I would gladely steal from V20 as I started to since I started playing V20. Also the suggestion for the roll helps a bit, I like it. Thank you very much there.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 gives you free XP. The expanded Diablerie rules from DSotBH give you free dots. <br /> <br /> That's very similar, but the latter is faster. I'm not as familiar with V5, but is there a reason why it has to be XP rather than just dots?<br /> <br /> I guess the benefit is that it lets you increase Blood Potency as well as Disciplines, but I'd just split the difference and raise your Blood Potency to the halfway point between yours and your victim's (or the minimum BP for your Generation if that's higher).<br /> <br /> Either way, I don't think it breaks game balance. By saying 'take one dot in a Discipline and one in a Skill' you can control their progression a bit better and avoid min-maxing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the +6 dots I actually do agree thinking about it. If you wanted to allow high attribute dots then you could either the VTR route or traditional route for a V5 solution. If you go the VTR route then it is simple as looking at Blood Potency, and allowing their rating maximum to be equal to their Blood Potency to a minimum of 5. Example: A kindred with Blood Potency of 7 can have up to 7 points worth of dots. If their Blood Potency weakens because of time in torpor, which can happen, the rating does not lower. This is how VTR did it, and I kinda like it.<br /> <br /> Obviously traditional route is to use the generation chart from old editions and using it for the maximum. </div> </div> </div>I like the BP=max trait thing, too. That also works and probably makes more sense in a V5 game, since Generation just sets minimum and maximum BP anyway. But you'd need to check the numbers (e.g., I think 8th Gens would be able to get 6s this way, although that's not the end of the world).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T11:59:48-07:00","id":1455035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1455033#post1455033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 gives you free XP. The expanded Diablerie rules from DSotBH give you free dots.<br /> <br /> That's very similar, but the latter is faster. I'm not as familiar with V5, but is there a reason why it has to be XP rather than just dots?</div> </div> </div> </div>IDK why it is from a design perspective, but from RAW in V5 there is a rule for gaining and losing advantage dots specifically. To summarize, if you gain a dot in an advantage, a merit or background, you lose it after the story is over unless you spend EXP to keep it. This is because in V5 advantages cost 3 exp per dot to get after character creation, likely to give players more agency in how their story develops or something IDK.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you lose an advantage/flaw, yes to also applies to flaws, you'll either get to pick another advantage or get a refund in EXP or dots depending on if you spent EXP on it or got it in Character creation.<br /> <br /> Most STs for V5 specifically will apply these rules to other things as well, but nothing else in V5 gets temporary dots other then advantages and disciplines for Thin-Bloods, which only lasts between feedings, so it doesn't tend to come up much.<br /> <br /> So if I had to guess why they don't give away free dots is to give a sense of game balance even if you can get EXP whenever the ST wants to have it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-16T23:34:36-07:00","id":1455066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1455035#post1455035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IDK why it is from a design perspective, but from RAW in V5 there is a rule for gaining and losing advantage dots specifically. To summarize, if you gain a dot in an advantage, a merit or background, you lose it after the story is over unless you spend EXP to keep it. This is because in V5 advantages cost 3 exp per dot to get after character creation, likely to give players more agency in how their story develops or something IDK.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, if you lose an advantage/flaw, yes to also applies to flaws, you'll either get to pick another advantage or get a refund in EXP or dots depending on if you spent EXP on it or got it in Character creation.<br /> <br /> Most STs for V5 specifically will apply these rules to other things as well, but nothing else in V5 gets temporary dots other then advantages and disciplines for Thin-Bloods, which only lasts between feedings, so it doesn't tend to come up much.<br /> <br /> So if I had to guess why they don't give away free dots is to give a sense of game balance even if you can get EXP whenever the ST wants to have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it. So presumably they hand out the XP so that Diablerie isn't an exception to the usual rule that you have to spend XP to lock in Advantages. That makes sense. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T11:21:27-07:00","id":1455580,"title":"","content":"You can improve the diablerie by nerfing the blood potency table. If young vampires have more distance to get blood potency, diablerie is more tempting. It's just an idea.<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Generation</b></td> <td colspan=\"3\" class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Blood potency max.</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">11th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">12th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">13th</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">14th+</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">0</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Oficial </b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><b>Option A </b></span></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Option B </span></b></td> </tr> </table></div> <i><span style=\"font-size:10px\">Sorry, my English is very bad.</span></i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26793,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","user":"Slasher","date":". 07-25-2021, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","name":"Slasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T11:59:22-07:00","id":1455582,"title":"","content":"Which reminds me.<br /> <br /> Blood potency is mechanical cancer in V5. You really don't want it beyond a certain amount (I think it was 5, but i haven't looked at the table). The Drawbacks far outweigh the merits. If you want Diablerie to be desirable, you need to curb these side effects and make Generation/potency a more-pros-than-cons deal. Reduce/Axe how hard it is for high potency vampires to sate hunger, reduce/axe bane severity.<br /> <br /> <br /> You should also get rid of TBA, or at least port TBA into blood sorcery that anyone can learn. You absolutely don't want TB's to have a comfortable little nieche for them to occupy. The TB's aren't meant to be in a happy place, mechanically they need to be encouraged to eat their way up, or to try and become human again. Giving them 3/4 discipline caps again might be the foundation they need to become invested in the vampire system and give them the impetus to diablerise when they hit their early limits. Scrapping the &quot;you get a clan when you eat up&quot; rule is also wise. Having them remain Caitiff when they reach 13th gen is also good, since Caitiffs are mechanically advantaged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-25-2021, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T12:52:23-07:00","id":1455584,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:16px\"><u><b>Alternative Feeding Penalty</b></u></span><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Blood Potency</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\"><b>Feeding Penalty</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">0</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">No effect</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">No effect</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">No effect</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Animal and bagged blood slakes half Hunger</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Animal and bagged blood slakes no Hunger</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Animal and bagged blood slakes no Hunger<br /> Slake 1 less Hunger per human</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Animal and bagged blood slakes no Hunger<br /> Slake 1 less Hunger per human<br /> Must drain and kill a human to reduce Hunger below 2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Animal and bagged blood slakes no Hunger<br /> Slake 2 less Hunger per human<br /> Must drain and kill a human to reduce Hunger below 2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Animal and bagged blood slakes no Hunger<br /> Slake 2 less Hunger per human<br /> Must drain and kill a human to reduce Hunger below 2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Animal and bagged blood slakes no Hunger<br /> Slake 2 less Hunger per human<br /> Must drain and kill a human to reduce Hunger below 3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 0px\">Human, Animal and bagged blood slakes no Hunger<br /> Must drain, kill a diablerize a vampire to reduce Hunger below 3</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <i>* Very powerful vampire blood can reduce hunger to 0.</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","name":"Slasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-25T23:28:11-07:00","id":1455597,"title":"","content":"I think tying Banes to Humanity rather than Blood Potency would be better if you need to make Diablerie more appealing. It's all drawbacks with Blood Potency as is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T09:36:07-07:00","id":1455618,"title":"","content":"Humanity 10: Decrease your blood potency 3 levels to use the Feeding Penalty.<br /> Humanity 9: Decrease your blood potency by 2 levels to use the Feeding Penalty.<br /> Humanity 8: Decrease your blood potency by 2 levels to use the Feeding Penalty.<br /> Humanity 7: Decrease your blood potency by 1 level to use the Feeding Penalty.<br /> Humanity 6: Decrease your blood potency by 1 level to use the Feeding Penalty.<br /> Humanity 5 to 3: No changes.<br /> Humanity 2: Increase your blood potency by 1 level to use the Feeding Penalty. (If it exceeds BP 10 it only satisfies with diablerie)<br /> Humanity 1: Increase your blood potency 2 level to use the Feeding Penalty. (If it exceeds BP 10 it only satisfies with diablerie)<br /> <br /> You can regulate humanity, blood potency with small changes and house rules.<br /> These are just ideas or examples","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26793-slasher","name":"Slasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-26T10:09:55-07:00","id":1455619,"title":"","content":"I think you could detach bane severity from Blood Potency effectively if you use this system instead:<br /> <br /> Your bane severity is (8-Humanity, minimum 1).<br /> <br /> VTR has banes usually affect you by applying a (10-Humanity) dice penalty or capping dice pools at your Humanity score, so this is a bit less punitive than that, and gives another incentive to maintain Humanity without undermining Diablerie as a fast and dangerous route to power.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-30T11:04:50-07:00","id":1455803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1455619#post1455619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you could detach bane severity from Blood Potency effectively if you use this system instead:<br /> <br /> Your bane severity is (8-Humanity, minimum 1).<br /> <br /> VTR has banes usually affect you by applying a (10-Humanity) dice penalty or capping dice pools at your Humanity score, so this is a bit less punitive than that, and gives another incentive to maintain Humanity without undermining Diablerie as a fast and dangerous route to power.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is cool, but I think just taking the Bane Severity from the Blood Potency charts and reversing them is enough. I actually decided to make a simple charts for this.<br /> <div align=\"center\"><i><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Humanity and Bane Severity (Pre Companion)</span></b></i></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Humanity Score</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Bane Severity</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">10</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">9</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">8</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">7</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">6</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">4</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">5</td> </tr> </table></div> This would make a falling Humanity much more interesting in addition to the normal effects from a degenerating Humanity. That said if this char is used here are a few exceptions:<br /> <br /> <b>Thin-Bloods and Caitiffs. </b>Any vampire without a clan bane does not need to worry about Bane severity at all. Thin-Bloods with the <b><i>Clan Curse</i></b> flaw are always considered to have a Bane Severity of 1 regardless of their Humanity Score.<br /> <br /> <b>Post Companion Update.</b> To update this chart with Bane Severity changes from the V5 Companion, simply increase the listed Bane Severity by 1.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>"