hout a clan bane does not need to worry about Bane severity at all. Thin-Bloods with the <b><i>Clan Curse</i></b> flaw are always considered to have a Bane Severity of 1 regardless of their Humanity Score.<br /> <br /> <b>Post Companion Update.</b> To update this chart with Bane Severity changes from the V5 Companion, simply increase the listed Bane Severity by 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>That works, too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T04:30:44-07:00","id":1456225,"title":"","content":"A mechanic our gm uses in 20th is to get a dot in the victims Disciplines unless you outclass them by a substantial margin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T08:56:12-07:00","id":1456244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1456225#post1456225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A mechanic our gm uses in 20th is to get a dot in the victims Disciplines unless you outclass them by a substantial margin.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly this would not work in v5 due to the fact v5 wants you to spend exp to get stuff. Anything you get for free goes away at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T11:05:58-07:00","id":1456252,"title":"","content":"V5 gives you the possibility of permanent xp from resonance. Which means that if you find the right juicebags or apply a good processing technique to some poor sap and agressively make it your goal to acquire premium food you can theoretically get absurd amounts of xp in downtime. That said, Humanity remains prohibitively expensive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-06T13:26:39-07:00","id":1456258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1456252#post1456252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V5 gives you the possibility of permanent xp from resonance. Which means that if you find the right juicebags or apply a good processing technique to some poor sap and agressively make it your goal to acquire premium food you can theoretically get absurd amounts of xp in downtime. That said, Humanity remains prohibitively expensive.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well yes, but actually no. Resonances themselves can't give XP, but Dyscrasias can, kinda. Okay so Dyscrasias, to put it simply, are effects individuals with an Acute resonance has in their blood that a vampire can tap for a bonus. This effect can only be obtained by sipping on the victims blood over the course of 3 nights or just draining them dry, gaining stains as a result. This bonus lasts until the next feeding or reaching Hunger 5, basically while the blood is in your system.<br /> <br /> Now there is only a 1% chance that anyone will have a naturally occurring instance of an Acute resonance. So it's more reasonable to farm for it instead, which is actually possible with the Herd background and/or a Project, likely getting stains due to the more effective methods of farming for it. However, the problem is that a Dyscrasia is given to the player by the Storyteller, and out of the samples given in the book only one of each resonance type actually gives XP. Not only that, but they only give 1 XP towards disciplines associated with the resonance the Dyscrasia derives.<br /> <br /> All this in mind, Dyscrasias are better spent trying to get their situational bonuses they can provide, like extra dice for pools and the like. Their natural rarity makes them gems when randomly found, but attempting to use them to XP farm disciplines is like trying to get a one of a kind drop over and over again. You can do it, but it's gonna be more effective to just spend your downtime doing other stuff.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T00:47:09-07:00","id":1456285,"title":"","content":"You get the XP, it's yours. That's the resonance used up. You aren't given five days to use your temporary XP. I'm going to take the rest of what you say at face value since I don't care to pick up that book again. <br /> Anyhow. A 1% chance is a very good amount for vampires if you assume they drink once a night, they should on average pick up at least three resonance providing juicebags a year. and vampires are likely to find &quot;Dyscrasias&quot; suitable for them given that different resonances are biased towards appropriate feeding types (you're going to find more &quot;sanguine&quot; stalking the club as a cassanova, which will grant presence, which is what you want. (Oh you can get blood magic from Sanguine which entirely laughs in the face of Tremere but that's more... I won't go there) and it's entirely possible for vampires to whip a person into shape and enhance a resonance into an accute one. <br /> <br /> So you pick up, let's say one Dysc every four months. You would be wise to put a lot of effort into putting this person in your herd. We've then got a lot of storyteller decisions we need to sus out, because the rules IIRC aren't so comprehensive. When can you feed from the same person again, do they have the same Dysc bonus or is it random every time you feed from them? these will tell you how reliably you can get XP. Perhaps you can feed from the same character and get a 1/7 chance of XP every three days, or perhaps you need to find the 1/7 dysc that consistantly puts out XP, or perhaps you need to wait a few months between feedings. By the time you're 10, you could have 30 dysc herd members, and by the time you're 50, you could have the cream-of-the-crop from150 dysc (or a more managable 21 if Dysc stay consistent and you're only looking for the 1/7 who grant XP) <br /> <br /> In the most ideal white-room ruling, an average 10 year old vampire can get an average of 4xp every 3 days, or 122xp per year exclusively for disciplines. This of course doubles for a 20 year old vampire, but quickly gets unwieldy unless we go for unchanging dyscrasias (which benefits elders at the expense of neonates). This doesn't account for rival vampires trying to poach your herd or vice versa or your herd escaping/dying, and of course I'm not caring about you not getting the ideal resonances. <br /> More conservatively, perhaps the storyteller decides you can only gain the best effects of blood every 3 months (supposedly the average time to recover from donating blood). In this case you gain, at 10 years an average of16xp per year. . <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T09:08:02-07:00","id":1456304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vilenecromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1456244#post1456244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadly this would not work in v5 due to the fact v5 wants you to spend exp to get stuff. Anything you get for free goes away at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah but that's the best part about home brew-what v5 'wants' isnt relavent what works is . It's why the first rule change of my prep for running v5 was to re-seperate Necromancy and Obtenerbration after I'd stopped laughing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-07T09:55:47-07:00","id":1456307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1454992-v5-more-tempting-diablerie-homebrew?p=1456285#post1456285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When can you feed from the same person again, do they have the same Dysc bonus or is it random every time you feed from them?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You have to safely feed three times over three nights to get the Dyscrasia, and even then it'll likely go away forever. Once tapped, the Dyscrasia leaves the blood in most cases, it rarely sticks after being obtained. If it does stick around then it's the same every time, but risks getting used up with every successful tap.<br /> <br /> The only reliable way to get a Dyscrasia is to train someone, which involves sever conditioning so they experience the same emotion and resonance so often that it gives you what you want. Once you taste your preferred Dyscrasia it will give you a name, which hints at what conditions you need to recreate. This part can be very dark, and border on abuse at times, I recommend it for certain power-hungry kindred or Sabbat, Sabbat would 100% do these things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><div align=\"left\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/7.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26764-vilenecromancer","name":"Vilenecromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26764_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"247"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}